   "k": "j6k4di",
   "en": "Strategies and guides"
  },
  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "13ukua9",
   "en": "Overview of the Carpatho-Ukraine nation"
  },
  {
   "k": "1fpe7tj",
   "en": "Carpatho-Ukraine can only be played with Ironman turned off, as since it cannot be spawned without using console commands. However, it can spawn via an event through phases of the partition of Czechoslovakia. Right after Slovakia's independence."
  },
  {
   "k": "3xcihe",
   "en": "Country creation"
  },
  {
   "k": "g044s3",
   "en": "In order to play as early as Carpatho-Ukraine, you would have to spawn it via console commands with either manually adding cores to release it with its tag ⟦0⟧, have it own states by manually doing the setowner RUT command then tag RUT to switch, or by annexing any country to Carpatho-Ukraine with the command annex CZE RUT to annex Czechoslovakia.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "1duj28s",
   "en": "RUT"
  },
  {
   "k": "1vrz2lb",
   "en": "Otherwise, by historical or random scenarios, wait until Germany starts the Sudetenland crisis. With the Carpatho-Ukraine independent, it starts with a few cores on the Polish states of Ukraine. And with the Carpathian Rus state as their independent state."
  },
  {
   "k": "5t2a8c",
   "en": "Surviving as Carpatho-Ukraine"
  },
  {
   "k": "1caogwv",
   "en": "Unlike some releasable nations, Carpatho-Ukraine doesn't get to core all of Ukrainian lands. As mentioned above that the nation starts as an OPM, with cores on Polish states of Ukraine. And with a democratic government, it wont last much. So the options here are switching to communist or fascist ideologies. With the fascist case, and TAOG DLC, add an HQ command unit to get one extra (but weak) unit to secure the border with Hungary. Watch for any Transylvanian events, as Hungary will try to go around you to capture your capital and small towns. Work on the political branch through the fascist path, make haste in order to have Germany accept you into their faction before Hungary does. Then, research and build land forts in order to endure and resist any attacks by the Hungarian army. It will take time for the Germans to accept you to the faction, but as long as your government is fascist, it will invite you to their faction. But, with the war going on with the Hungarians, they'll reluctantly join the war. But if there are allies such as Italy, Protektorat Bohmen or Romania, accept their offer and they'll provide the heavy lifting."
  },
  {
   "k": "6n7qod",
   "en": "The same can also apply with communism, discard the government, build land forts, hold an referendum and finally become a communist OPM nation. And subsequently join the Comintern. Another bonus that works on the minor nation's favor is the weekly manpower. It fills the militia units manpower. As with the Hungarian menace, calling the soviet union when in war, they'll rush in to lift up the siege. The only thing that remains is if Hungary joins or doesn't join the Axis. Ideally, if Hungary doesn't join the Axis, yet, then the entire Comintern will do the work with you."
  },
  {
   "k": "ml2l3h",
   "en": "Re-Establishing the Republic of Ukraine"
  },
  {
   "k": "9bixyy",
   "en": "Perhaps to make up for the lack of decision you can console command core Ukrainian lands in Poland, Soviet Union and Romania. Depending on your pick the fascist or communist and rely on your allies, the idea is to reunite all of the Ukrainian cores under the Carpatho-Ukraine rule. If in Axis, Carpatho-Ukraine should take the Ukrainian cores from Poland. And in war with the Soviet Union, go for the Ukrainian cores, including Bucovina and Southern Bessarabia, if they've taken them from the Romanians."
  },
